.TH PODSHL-REPAIRS 1 2026-09-19 "podshl-repairs 0.1.8" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
podshl-repairs \- keep a record of local fixes, and look at them again after updates
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B podshl-repairs
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B podshl-repairs
.RB [ \-\-version | \-V ]
.RB [ \-\-help | \-h ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
A local fix outlives its reason.
The bug it works around gets fixed upstream, an update overwrites it, or a
cloned plugin keeps running while the packaged one moves on, and a year later
nobody knows why it is there.
.B podshl-repairs
keeps a record of such changes and looks at them again after every update or
once a day.
.PP
It
.B never removes or undoes anything by itself.
A newer version is a reason to look, not proof that a fix can go: a backport
and a fix that did not hold look the same from here.
.PP
Records come from three places:
.IP \(bu 2
a person, a script or an agent registering a change
.RB ( add ,
or
.B begin
and
.B done
around it);
.IP \(bu 2
a coding agent's own hooks, which record what it writes outside git
repositories
.RB ( install\-agent\-hook );
.IP \(bu 2
packages and Omarchy plugins that declare why they leave the ordinary path;
see
.BR podshl\-repairs.d (5).
.PP
Every field a decision reads is written by code: versions come from the
package manager, paths are resolved, digests are computed.
A note or a reason is kept and shown, and nothing reads it.
.PP
Every command also answers
.B \-\-help
without running.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR review " [" \-\-json "] [" \-\-notify "] [" \-\-offline ]
What wants another look, and why: a file changed since the fix or gone, the
copy an undo needs gone, a package updated or frozen behind the official one,
what an override stands in front of changed, an upstream issue closed or its
fix released, a declaration withdrawn by its maintainer or its package
removed.
Takes in what installed packages and plugins declare first.
.B \-\-notify
also shows a desktop notification; on Omarchy it stays until dismissed and
a click opens the review in a terminal.
.B \-\-offline
asks nobody, not even about watched issues.
.TP
.BR list " [" \-\-json ]
Every record.
.TP
.BR show " " \fIID\fR " [" \-\-json ]
Everything about one record: its state, why it was made \(em the note, or the
maintainer's reason for a declared one \(em who declared it and whether that
was withdrawn, the upstream issue and whether it is watched, the version with
the fix, whether there is a copy to go back to, and when it was recorded.
.TP
.BR add " \-\-kind " file | package | overlay " \-\-by " \fINAME\fR " [" options ]
Record a change that has already been made.
Nothing is kept to go back to.
Options:
.BI \-\-path " P"
(file, overlay),
.BI \-\-package " NAME"
(package),
.BI \-\-original " P"
and
.BI \-\-original\-package " NAME"
(overlay: what the copy stands in front of),
.BI \-\-issue " URL"
(the upstream issue or pull request),
.BI \-\-fixed\-in " V"
(the first version with the fix),
.B \-\-watch
(ask GitHub about the issue),
.BI \-\-note " TEXT".
.TP
.BR begin " \-\-kind file \-\-by " \fINAME\fR " \-\-path " \fIP\fR " [" options ]
Before changing a file: keep a copy of it and print the record's id.
.TP
.BI done " ID"
The change announced by
.B begin
is made; its digest is taken now.
.TP
.BI keep " ID"
Looked at, and kept: what was shown is not raised again until something
changes.
.TP
.BI watch " ID " on | off
Ask GitHub about the record's issue, at most once a day, straight to its
public API and never through anybody else.
Off unless switched on per record: each lookup tells GitHub which issue this
machine follows.
.TP
.BI restore " ID"
Put back the copy
.B begin
kept.
.TP
.BI forget " ID"
Remove what a record said.
Needs administrator or root rights and the id typed back at a real terminal;
no option skips either.
A stub stays, saying that a record existed and when it was removed.
.TP
.BR install\-hook " [" \-\-print ]
.TQ
.BR remove\-hook " [" \-\-print ]
Run
.B review \-\-notify
after every Omarchy update (a post\-update hook), or once a day elsewhere (a
systemd user timer, a launchd agent, a scheduled task).
.B \-\-print
says what would be done and does nothing.
.TP
.BR install\-agent\-hook " [" \-\-agent " " \fINAME\fR "] [" \-\-print ]
.TQ
.BR remove\-agent\-hook " [" \-\-agent " " \fINAME\fR "] [" \-\-print ]
Record what a coding agent writes outside git repositories, through the
agent's own hooks: a copy before each file write or shell command, the
record finished after it, one record per file per session.
A shell command is seen through the files it names.
On Omarchy the default agent is taken unless one is named.
Measured for
.B claude
only; other agents are refused by name.
Everything else in the agent's settings is kept, and the change to them is
itself recorded.
.TP
.BR agent\-hook " " pre | post " [" \-\-agent " " \fINAME\fR ]
What the agent's hooks call, with the agent's own JSON on standard input.
Always exits 0: a record missed is a gap, an agent stopped by one is a
removed tool.
.TP
.BR \-\-version ", " \-V
The version.
.TP
.BR help ", " \-\-help ", " \-h
The commands.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Nothing to look at, or the command did what it was asked.
.TP
.B 3
.B review
found something to look at.
.TP
.B 1
An error; the reason is on standard error.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/podshl/repairs.json
The record.
.TP
.I ~/.config/podshl/backups/
The copies
.B begin
keeps.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/podshl/client.log
What every command that changes something did, anonymised.
.TP
.I ~/.config/omarchy/hooks/post\-update.d/podshl\-repairs
The Omarchy update hook.
.TP
.I /usr/share/podshl/repairs.d/ ~/.local/share/podshl/repairs.d/ ~/.config/omarchy/plugins/*/repairs.d/
Declarations; see
.BR podshl\-repairs.d (5).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B VS_ROOT
Keep the record somewhere else.
.TP
.B PODSHL_LOG=0
Write no log.
.TP
.B CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR
Where Claude Code keeps its settings, when not
.IR ~/.claude .
.SH EXAMPLES
Record a change before making it, and undo it:
.PP
.nf
.RS
id=$(podshl\-repairs begin \-\-kind file \-\-by me \-\-path ~/.config/app/app.conf)
# ... change the file ...
podshl\-repairs done "$id"
podshl\-repairs restore "$id"
.RE
.fi
.PP
A package built locally until an upstream fix is released, watched:
.PP
.nf
.RS
podshl\-repairs add \-\-kind package \-\-by me \-\-package hyprland \e
    \-\-issue https://github.com/hyprwm/Hyprland/pull/1234 \-\-watch
.RE
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR podshl\-repairs.d (5),
.BR podshl\-client (1)
.PP
https://github.com/dx111ge/podshl/blob/main/docs/REPAIRS.md
